title "From sound to meaning"
layout layered dir=down
page a3
font 8pt..36pt wrap=16em

style form color=#1565C0
style structure color=#EF6C00
style meaning color=#6A1B9A

node sounds "Speech signal" .form
| continuous acoustic information
| pressure waves vary in time and frequency
node phon "Phonology" .form
| contrastive sound categories
| phonemes contrast in a language-specific system
node words "Morphology" .structure
| roots, affixes, and word formation
| morphemes carry grammatical or lexical meaning
node lexicon "Lexicon" .structure
| stored words and constructional patterns
| frequency affects access and change
node syntax "Syntax" .structure
| constituents and grammatical relations
| recursion creates unbounded combinations
node prosody "Prosody" .form
| stress, rhythm, and intonation
| signals boundaries and discourse focus
node context "Discourse context" .structure
| speaker, listener, and shared knowledge
| prior turns constrain interpretation
node semantics "Semantics" .meaning
| compositional sentence meaning
| truth conditions combine lexical meanings
node pragmatics "Pragmatics" .meaning
| intended meaning in context
| implicature can exceed literal content
node interpretation "Interpretation" .meaning
| listener integrates form, structure, and context
| ambiguity is resolved probabilistically
node variation "Language variation" .meaning
| dialects differ in sound, grammar, and lexicon
| variation is systematic, not random noise
node change "Language change" .meaning
| usage patterns diffuse across speakers
| sound change can be regular and gradual

sounds -> phon
sounds -> prosody
phon -> words
words -> syntax
words -> lexicon
syntax -> semantics
context -> pragmatics
semantics -> pragmatics
pragmatics -> interpretation
prosody -> interpretation
lexicon -> interpretation
syntax ..> context "depends on context"
variation ..> sounds "community norms"
variation ..> syntax "community norms"
change ..> variation "historical source"

require sounds at top
require interpretation at bottom
prefer context near pragmatics within=12em weight=3
prefer prosody near sounds within=14em weight=2
